<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo Sept crude oil imports up threefold vs August.</title>
<headline>Yugo Sept crude oil imports up threefold vs August.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslav crude oil imports rose nearly threefold in September to 217,104 tonnes from 71,909 tonnes in August, the Federal Statistics office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The imports were worth $36 million against $12 million the previous month.</p>
<p>Imports of oil products rose to 40,637 tonnes from 27,635 tonnes in August and were worth $12 million.</p>
<p>Cummulative January-September crude imports stood at 575,051 tonnes and were worth $93 million.</p>
<p>Oil product imports in the same period totalled 922,648 tonnes and were worth $202 million.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
</text>
